GIT PUSH
========

Upload your commits to remote repository.


BASIC
-----
git push

Sends your commits to GitHub/GitLab.


WHAT IT DOES
------------
• Uploads your commits
• Updates remote branch
• Shares your work


WHEN TO USE
-----------
After committing your changes.
When ready to share with others.


OPTIONS
-------
Push to specific branch:
  git push origin main

Force push (careful!):
  git push --force

Push new branch:
  git push -u origin feature-name


ERRORS
------
"rejected"           → Pull first, then push
"no remote"          → Add remote with git remote add
"permission denied"  → Check your access rights
